From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolai Semendiaev <agent00791@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:42:32 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: use private page-frag caches for RXDMA rings

Based on Mark Ruvald Pedersen's ath11k per-ring page-frag isolation.
Regular RX and monitor buffers currently share per-CPU caches with other
network users. Long-lived ring fragments can retain sparsely populated
32-KiB backing pages even while ring occupancy remains constant.

Give each regular and monitor RXDMA ring a private page_frag_cache.
Preserve initial skb headroom, allocation flags and DMA
map/unmap operations. Existing refill SRNG locks serialize the private
caches.
Drain monitor caches after their IDR-owned buffers are released and the
regular RX cache after its cookie-conversion descriptors are released.
Quiesce external IRQ/NAPI processing before non-reset crash teardown;
the reset worker already does so. The IRQ lifecycle patch is required.

Keep the original series' DMA-alignment correction: skb_pull() cannot
advance an empty skb, so use skb_reserve() before posting each buffer.
Reserve extra alignment space for monitor status buffers so that their
DMA capacity remains at least RX_MON_STATUS_BUF_SIZE after alignment.
RX ring capacities and CE allocation remain unchanged.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/20260719215817.2468580-4-wabsie@gmail.com/
Signed-off-by: Nikolai Semendiaev <agent00791@gmail.com>
---
